course: dictionary
lesson: 12869
title: Words for people who ask
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An enquirer is a person who asks for information about something. Enquire and ask mean nearly the same, but enquirer is a more formal word, so you will often see it in letters, offices and shops. «Every enquirer will receive a reply within ten days.» The writer means: everyone who asks will get an answer.
explain: The word has a second, more formal meaning: someone who looks into a question to find out the truth. «The curious enquirer studied the old maps for weeks.» Here the enquirer is not just asking; they are investigating. Read the words around it to find which meaning fits.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence. «A curious enquirer asks lots of questions about the stars.» Curious tells you the enquirer wants to learn, and asks lots of questions tells you what they do. When you meet enquirer, ask yourself: is this person asking, or looking into something carefully?
fact: An enquirer is a person who asks for information.
fact: «Enquirer» is a noun. One is an enquirer; several are enquirers.
fact: In formal letters you may see «all enquirers», which means every person who asks.
fact: «Enquirer» can also mean someone who investigates or looks into a question.
fact: In the US the usual spelling is «inquirer»; both spellings mean the same thing.
exercise: «The enquirer asked the museum guide when the dinosaurs arrived.» What is an enquirer? | A large dinosaur | *A person who asks for information | A ticket for the bus | A museum that is closed
exercise: Which word in «Every enquirer will receive a reply» means a person who asks? | receive | every | reply | *enquirer
exercise: «The curious enquirer wanted to know why the sky is blue.» What does curious mean here? | Very tall | *Eager to know or learn | Angry with someone | Sleepy after a long day
test: «The enquirer rang the library to ask about opening times.» Who rang the library? | A clock on the wall | *A person asking for information | A book about history | The librarian who works there
test: In a formal letter, «All enquirers will receive a reply.» What does this tell you? | Only people with money get a reply | *People who ask questions will get an answer | Enquirers must write a poem | Nobody will ever reply
exam: «The curious enquirer looked carefully into the question until she found the answer.» What does enquirer mean here? | A person who is always late | *A person who looks into a question to find the truth | A question that has no answer | A shop that sells maps
